{"success": true, "name": "arc-grid-solving", "file": "references/repeated-motif-extension.md", "content": "# Repeated motif, continuation, and extension: review notes

A single demonstration showed a structured foreground motif repeated in a second location; only a region at the later instance's edge changed to color 1. Other demonstrations showed the same broad palette but dissimilar geometry and localized changed regions. This does not establish a reliable shared operation by itself: the hypothesis that color 1 simply fills a horizontal run from the rightmost marks failed on the test, as did a second attempt that filled apparent gaps between sparse cells.

